# Wave W17-Y (Route 213): salt sand — lakefront pale sand, design-authorised: a pale sand slightly greyed by the salt it crosses, running Fenland to the Gallant shore under the boat racks (design: the shore road climbing through the flats to the hotels on the hill). Split from Lake Gallant’s shore sand beside it by the grey entire — flat-crossed vs shore-washed — and from Route 209’s bell sand by temperature: pilgrims’ cool grey vs salt grey.
